<!--
  In-APK Remote Config defaults, used before the first successful fetch and whenever the
  device is offline.

  Deliberately empty. All three parameters this app reads — `ad_ids`, `ad_rules` and
  `native_config` — are JSON blobs, and RemoteConfigManager already falls back to the Kotlin
  data-class defaults in `remoteconfig/data/RemoteConfigData.kt` when the fetched string is
  blank. Duplicating those here would create a second source of truth that silently drifts
  from the first.

  Ad unit ids have their own offline fallback in `res/values/ad_units.xml`, which is what
  serves on a first cold start — see AdUnits.kt.

  Kept wired up (RemoteConfigManager still calls setDefaultsAsync) so that a scalar key which
  genuinely needs an in-APK default has an obvious home: getLong()/getBoolean() return
  0/false when no default exists, which is rarely the safe value.
-->
<defaultsMap />
